# Trello Clone — Project Rules

## Architecture Boundaries
- Frontend (repo root, Vercel) and backend (server/,Render) are separate deployments. Never import backend code into frontend..
- The Node.js + Socket.io server on Render is the ONLY backend. Never use Next.js API routes for WebSocket or for board data..
- Do NOT use Supabase, Firebase, or any external database service. The JSON file on Render's persistent disk is the ONLY source of truth..

## Socket.io Conventions
- The Socket.io client must be a singleton. Never create multiple io() instances — always import the shared instance from lib/socket.ts..
- Always optimistic update local state BEFORE emitting socket events..
- Handle socket disconnect gracefully — show connection UI state, never crash..
- Keep drag-and-drop logic isolated from socket logic: Board.tsx handles DnD, page.tsx handles socket events and state..
- All socket event handlers on the server must wrap logic in try/catch and report errors via socket error events..

## Storage & Deployment
- JSON file path must stay relative and inside the data/ directory for Render persistent-disk compatibility (fs.mkdirSync data/ on boot).
- CORS must allow all origins for Render-Vercel communication..
- The server seeds board.json automatically on first boot if missing..

## TypeScript
- Use TypeScript strict mode..
- Define interfaces for Task, Column, and BoardData..
- Never use 'any'. Define proper types for socket event payloads..
- Use the @/* path alias for imports inside frontend (root** files where applicable..

## Quality
- No placeholder functions, empty handlers, or TODO comments..
- All user-facing copy must be in English..